+// Durable origin (R03 B17, 2026-10-27; B16 case 2: a guest whose game closed 5.8 s after the summon
+// woke in its own world at the HOST's spot - a level-10 Clinic character in Cathedral Ward). After a
+// crash the journal's home spot takes the character back to where it joined from, or to its recorded
+// lamp. It was behind SHADPS4_BBSC_EXPERIMENTAL_HOME_RECOVERY=1 because a pending return crossed from
+// one character to another after Quit Game -> title -> Load (A02). It is now bound to its owner:
+// armed only from RecoverBbscOwnWorldFile (the journal's save slot is the active one, PR #11), dropped
+// at any load from the title (NoteBbscOwnWorldCharacterLoad), and every step checks the active save
+// slot is still the owner's (TickBbscHomeRecovery). The journal file stays on disk until the return
+// settles, so a dropped return is taken up again by its owner. Each target is bounded: an accepted
+// request whose load never comes times out, a refused or missed point goes to the recorded lamp, and
+// an exhausted lamp (or point without a lamp) ends with the journal kept as .unreturned.
+// Still an opt-in candidate (SHADPS4_BBSC_HOME_RECOVERY=1, or the older experimental variable) until
+// the native gate in R03-B17-DURABLE-ORIGIN.md (N1 locked-map return, N2 title/other character, lamp
+// fallback with save/reload) has evidence on a matching build.
+constexpr int BbscHomeRecoveryMaxTries = 3;          // per target (point, then lamp)
+constexpr s64 BbscHomeRecoveryLoadTimeoutMs = 30'000; // accepted request, no load
+
+bool BbscHomeRecoveryOn() {
